// This example sets up the same basic Android project as xref:example/androidlib/kotlin/1-hello-kotlin.adoc[1-hello-kotlin],
// but configured declaratively via `build.mill.yaml`/`package.mill.yaml` files instead of a
// Scala `build.mill`. We utilize `AndroidAppKotlinModule` and `AndroidSdkModule` to streamline
// the process of building an Android application with minimal configuration.
//
//
// The Android SDK is configured as a nested `object androidSdkModule:` in the root
// `build.mill.yaml`. The app module then refers to it by path via the `androidSdkModule` key,
// the same way `moduleDeps` refers to other modules by path.

/** See Also: build.mill.yaml */
/** See Also: app/package.mill.yaml */
/** See Also: app/test/package.mill.yaml */
/** See Also: app/it/package.mill.yaml */

// Unlike the Scala variant, this example builds a debug APK rather than a signed release
// build: the release-signing fields aren't all `Task`-shaped, so they can't be set from YAML.
// Everything else works the same as the Scala version.

/** Usage

> ./mill show app.androidApk
".../out/app/androidApk.dest/app.apk"

> ./mill app.it.androidTestApk

> ./mill -j 1 show app.test
...Compiling 2 Kotlin sources...

> cat out/app/test/testForked.dest/worker-0/out.json
["",[...{"fullyQualifiedName":"com.helloworld.ExampleUnitTest.text_size_is_correct","selector":"com.helloworld.ExampleUnitTest.text_size_is_correct","duration":...,"status":"Success"}...]]

> cat out/app/test/testForked.dest/worker-0/out.json
["",[...{"fullyQualifiedName":"com.helloworld.ExampleUnitTestInKotlinDir.kotlin_dir_text_size_is_correct","selector":"com.helloworld.ExampleUnitTestInKotlinDir.kotlin_dir_text_size_is_correct","duration":...,"status":"Success"}...]]

*/